==English==
[[Image:Borage-flower-hr.jpg|thumb|''Borago officinalis'']]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|borage}} (compare French {{m|fr|bourrache}}), from {{etyl|Medieval Latin|en}} {{m|la|borrago}}, either from Latin {{m|la|borra||short wool, rough hair}} or {{etyl|ar|en}} {{m|ar|الأب من العرق||''abu min arak'', lit. father of sweat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbɒɹ.ɪdʒ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{taxlink|Borago officinalis|species|noshow=1}}, a [[Mediterranean]] [[plant]] with rough, cucumber-flavored leaves, used in [[salad]]s.

